    {
      "id": "w26ucwz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Effects of Volcanoes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y57odxk",
      "content": "• Formation of new landforms."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g7swfrn",
      "content": "• Creation of fertile soils due to volcanic ash."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6yyos0f",
      "content": "• Volcanic disasters destroying settlements.<img></img>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "inhaodf",
      "content": "• Emission of gases affecting climate."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Volcanoes and Earthquakes",
      "id": "wh2puvn"
    },
    {
      "id": "kzf58tf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Earthquakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1dj7f8w",
      "content": "An earthquake is the sudden shaking of the Earth's surface caused by the release of energy from movements within the Earth's crust. This energy travels in the form of seismic waves."
    },
    {
      "id": "nwnqoyk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Important Terms"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dhvyfkz",
      "content": "• Focus (Hypocenter) – point inside Earth where earthquake originates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nac0a19",
      "content": "• Epicenter – point on the surface directly above the focus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "czmta77",
      "content": "• Seismic Waves – energy waves produced during earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t4tllmf",
      "content": "• Fault – fracture in Earth's crust where movement occurs."
    },
    {
      "id": "efpt3vk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Seismic Waves"
    },
    {
      "id": "bfunlxy",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Wave</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Characteristics</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Medium</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>P Waves</p>",
            "<p>Fastest seismic waves</p>",
            "<p>Travel through solids, liquids and gases</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>S Waves</p>",
            "<p>Slower than P waves</p>",
            "<p>Travel only through solids</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>L Waves</p>",
            "<p>Surface waves causing maximum damage</p>",
            "<p>Travel along Earth's surface</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
